TITLE:: RCOrgnsm
summary:: An orgnsm: a beat template with identity, state and resources
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Guides/reCurrent, Classes/RCBatch, Classes/RCOrgnsmRegistry, Classes/RCPathControl, Classes/RCOrgnsmPatterns

DESCRIPTION::
An RCOrgnsm is a template; link::#-create:: returns a registered clone that is prepared (an link::Classes/RCBeatSpec::) and started with link::#-start::. Identity is species / tribe / number → name code::orgnsm_<species>_t<tribe>_<number>::, the beat name in its layer and the OSC instrument name.

State lives in link::#-staticAttrs:: (an Event, so computed entries code::{ |self| ... }:: work); patterns in link::#-attrDictBase:: read it through code::Pfunc { |ev| ev.self.staticAttrs.x }:: so edits take effect at the next event. Function-valued static attributes may be written code::{ }:: or, as before, code::{{ }}::.

Key paths (link::#-rPut:: / link::#-rGet::): a bare key addresses code::staticAttrs::; code::"attr_dict_base.x":: / code::"attrDictBase.x"::, code::"add_first_array_base.x":: / code::"addFirstArrayBase.x"::, code::"static_attrs.x"::, code::"server_ressources.x":: / code::"serverResources.x"::. A static attribute whose name shadows a method (code::release::, code::size::, code::value::...) is warned about: code::ev.release:: would call the method.

